module System/Numerics

# `/` divides as decimals: each side becomes a `Decimal` and the quotient is a `Decimal` (`7 / 2` is `3.5`). `//` and
# `%` stay the whole-number quotient and remainder.

### Divides as decimals: `7 / 2` is `3.5`, `1 / 3` is `0.3333…` to 34 significant digits.
### :param you: The divisor.
### :returns: The quotient as a `Decimal`.
### :throws: {DivisionByZeroError} when `you` is zero, and {NumericOverflowError} when a side has more significant
###     digits than a `Decimal` holds exactly (34).
failable routine Integer.truediv(you: Integer) -> Decimal
    return me.exact_decimal().truediv(you: you.exact_decimal())

### This value as a `Decimal`, which holds it exactly: 34 significant digits, trailing zeros aside.
### :returns: The same value as a `Decimal`.
### :throws: {NumericOverflowError} when the value has more significant digits than a `Decimal` holds.
secret failable routine Integer.exact_decimal() -> Decimal
    var digits = me.abs()
    var ten = 10
    if not digits.is_zero()
        until not (digits % ten).is_zero()
            digits = digits // ten
    if digits >= "10000000000000000000000000000000000".to[Integer]()
        throw NumericOverflowError(description: "the integer has more significant digits than a Decimal holds (34)")
    return me.to[Decimal]()
